# scripts/Films (12 October 2026)

Worker of the film queue of ZenRay Assets: archive upload, CMAF HLS and DASH packaging, subtitles, SHA-256 proof and unload of the local original. (12 October 2026)

- `ProcessFilmsSequentially.py`: the worker. It runs from the atelier `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-movies-series-upload/Scripts/`; this copy is the versioned reference. Edit here, copy to the atelier, restart at a boundary with `~/.claude/skills/zenray-progress/scripts/RestartFilmWorker.sh`. (12 October 2026)
- `BuildFilmsIndexMapping.py`, `IdentityShadowWatcher.py`, `PrepareSubtitleCopy.py`: helpers called by the worker. (12 October 2026)
- Knobs (environment, defaults in the code): `ZR_UPLOAD_FLOWS` 2, `ZR_UPLOAD_STAGGER_S` 20, `ZR_QUEUE_ORDER` small-first, `ZR_PACKAGE_FLOWS` 2, `ZR_VERIFY_FILMS` 5, `ZR_WINDOW` 8, `ZR_WINDOW_GIB` 45, `ZR_VERIFY_MODE` shadow, `ZR_DEFER_INDEX_ADD` 1, `ZR_REQUIRE_CLEAN_NAMES` off. (12 October 2026)
- Restart loses the archive uploads in flight (they are not resumable yet): restart just after an upload started, never in the middle of a large one. (12 October 2026)
- Tests: `scripts/Films/tests/` (`test_flush.py` with its stub `index-add-paths.mjs`, `test_dest.py`, `test_rounds.py`, `test_main_rounds.py`, `lanes_smoke.py`). They load the deployed worker from the atelier path and use fake subprocesses; run them with `python3 -I <test>.py` (`test_flush.py` takes the folder holding the stub as argument). (12 October 2026)
